# One finding ID per line (CVE, GHSA, AVD-DS-*, secret rule, license).
# Optional expiry suffix: ' exp:YYYY-MM-DD'. Audited suppressions carry a
# statement in docs/operations.md.
#
# --- python site-packages vendored inside oss-cad-suite (fpga-tools) ---
# The sha256-pinned OSS CAD Suite tarball ships its own python2.7 and
# python3.11 trees under /opt/oss-cad-suite/lib; the pinned release
# (2026-10-07) still vendors these interpreters, so the upstream-borne
# findings are expected to persist — the real fix is a future suite
# release that rebuilds its bundled pythons. They are waived per-CVE
# until 2027-01-03 and re-verified by the publish-gate Trivy scan on
# every OSS_CAD_SUITE_RELEASE bump
# (scripts/dependency_update_deferrals.json).
# Flask/Werkzeug serve no network endpoint in the image; pip/setuptools
# under the vendored pythons are never invoked by the fpga package.
CVE-2023-30861 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2024-34069 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2021-3572 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2022-40897 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2024-6345 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2027-01-03
#
# --- CIS baseline: build/CI tool images ---------------------------------
# DS-0002 (runs as root) and DS-0026 (no HEALTHCHECK): these images are CI
# build/tool containers, not deployed services. Non-root would change
# ownership of mounted workspace artifacts for no exploitable gain, and a
# HEALTHCHECK is meaningless for batch tooling (the publish and audit
# gates are the health checks). See docs/operations.md
# "Container hardening -> CIS baseline".
AVD-DS-0002 exp:2027-01-04
AVD-DS-0026 exp:2027-01-04
